>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC : simpExtLib.simp_mode ->
  simpExtLib.xsimptac_config -> simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> tactic
simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST :
  TraverseExt.child_first_policy -> simpExtLib.simp_mode ->
  simpExtLib.xsimptac_config -> simpExtLib.simpset -> thm list -> tactic
simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST_BOUND :
  TraverseExt.child_first_policy -> simpExtLib.simp_mode ->
  simpExtLib.xsimptac_config -> simpExtLib.simpset ->
  simpExtLib.rewrite_bundle -> thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Simplifies assumptions and conclusion together to a fixpoint.

``` hol4
type simptac_config =
  {strip : bool, elimvars : bool, droptrues : bool, oldestfirst : bool}
type xsimptac_config =
  {base : simptac_config, concl_in_fixpoint : bool,
   imp_rebuild : bool, imp_premises : bool}
```

These configuration types belong to `simpExtLib`. `#base cfg` controls
stripping simplified assumptions, eliminating variables by substitution,
dropping true assumptions and processing oldest assumptions first.

`GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC mode cfg ss ths` repeatedly simplifies assumptions with
the other selected assumptions, then simplifies the conclusion with the
solver/looper pipeline. Additional flags enable:

- `concl_in_fixpoint`: simplify the conclusion after each assumption pass;
  restart the passes if it changes.
- `imp_premises`: first attempt root rewriting of an implicational conclusion,
  then move antecedents into the assumptions.
- `imp_rebuild`: try root rewrites of implications rebuilt from the conclusion
  and assumptions (most recent first); restart after the first successful one.

Child-first traversal is opt-in. Supplied rules share invocation-wide bounded
controls across passes and branches. Solver contexts are untagged. `NoAsms`
and `IgnAsm` are respected by both bound and unbound global paths, including
recursive passes and options beneath bounded wrappers. The looper round
limit is shared across all conclusion/fixpoint reentry and sibling branches
in one invocation; applying a saved tactic again starts a fresh round budget.

For `BOUND`, install the bundle exactly once in the supplied invocation
simpset before calling the tactic. The bundle retains its untagged solver
context. Use the last argument for local directives; do not resupply the
bundle's rules there, which would compile them as additional rewrites.
Local replay preserves all installed controls, including partially spent or
exhausted ambient rules; `BOUND` never reinstalls or recompiles its bundle.
Attached views reuse their compiled matchers and share surviving controls.
Use an extension recipe from the start, not an ordinary simpset converted
at this boundary.

### Failure

May diverge. Invalid directives and failed requirements can raise `HOL_ERR`.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val cfg : simpExtLib.xsimptac_config =
     {base = {strip = true, elimvars = false,
              droptrues = true, oldestfirst = true},
      concl_in_fixpoint = true, imp_rebuild = false, imp_premises = true};
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} cfg
     ext_bool_ss [] ([], “x = 1 ⇒ y = x ⇒ P y”) c;
>>_ val policy = TraverseExt.charge_only (fn () => ());
>>_ val (base,args) = simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_arguments
     ext_bool_ss [BoundedRewrites.Once boolTheory.AND_CLAUSES];
>>_ val bundle = simpExtLib.prepare_rewrite_bundle base args;
>>_ val invocation = simpExtLib.install_rewrite_bundle bundle [] base;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_GLOBAL_SIMP_TAC_CHILD_FIRST_BOUND policy {safe = false}
     cfg invocation bundle [markerLib.NoAsms] ([], “p ∧ T”) c;
```

